    <h4>▶ PHASE 22 KEY INNOVATIONS FROM PHASE 21</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Miasma Temple Boiler Mark 1: entirely new flash boiler design replacing conventional 1-gallon unit — smaller, faster, more efficient</li>
      <li>Domed cube pressure vessel: 4 locomotive-style domed side faces handle pressure better than flat faces — same 1cm wall thickness but significantly higher pressure rating</li>
      <li>Hollow copper cascade pyramid: internal stepped pyramid with gravity-fed waterfall cascade — water falls top to bottom through 3 copper levels</li>
      <li>Internal heater coil: resistance coil wound inside hollow pyramid heats from core outward — all levels reach temperature simultaneously — much faster cold start</li>
      <li>Cone rivets on horizontal faces: break Leidenfrost vapor cushion on impact — cone tip penetrates vapor layer — water splits down cone sides maximizing flash contact</li>
      <li>Dome rivets on vertical and curved interior faces: break Leidenfrost layer for laterally-traveling droplets — dome crown contact point maximizes flash conversion</li>
      <li>High-pressure atomizing mist injection: 300 PSI mist replaces low-pressure EWI drip — breaks Leidenfrost at impact velocity — more complete flash conversion</li>
      <li>Steam outlets at top of front face with internal standpipes: only dry risen steam exits — no liquid water hammer risk in steam pipes to pistons</li>
      <li>10 gallon polypropylene tank: lighter, translucent level indicator, no rust, better rear packaging than 20 gal SS tank — condenser loop maintains near-infinite range</li>
      <li>Dual stage water filtration: 50 micron primary + 5 micron secondary before EWI — protects atomizing nozzle and boiler surface from scale buildup</li>
    </ul>
