<!-- TEMPLE BOILER DETAIL -->
<div class="panel" id="panel-temple">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--temple)">Diagram 2 · Miasma Temple Boiler Mark 1 — Full Detail</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Domed Cube Vessel · Hollow Copper Pyramid · Cone + Dome Rivets · Internal Heater · Standpipe Steam Outlets</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    The Miasma Temple Boiler Mark 1 is a half-gallon stainless 304 pressure vessel with four outward-domed side faces for superior pressure distribution — same principle as locomotive boiler barrel ends.
    Top and bottom faces remain flat: top for injection equipment mounting, bottom for pyramid seating and heater electrical feedthrough.
    Inside sits a hollow stepped copper pyramid in three cascade levels. Water mist from the high-pressure EWI injector falls by gravity from the top apex downward through the cascade.
    Each horizontal step face has cone rivets pointing upward to break the Leidenfrost vapor cushion on impact. Vertical faces and interior dome walls carry dome rivets for lateral droplet interception.
    The hollow pyramid contains an internal resistance heater coil wound in a spiral following the pyramid geometry — heating all levels simultaneously from the inside out.
    Steam rises naturally (counter-flow to falling water) and collects at the top of the vessel. Two 3/4 inch steam outlet ports on the upper front face each have internal standpipes — ensuring only dry fully-risen steam exits.
  </p>

