  <h2 class="section-title">10 Gallon Poly Tank · 24V Pump · Dual Stage Filter · High Pressure EWI · Condenser Return</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    Phase 22 water system is redesigned from Phase 21. The 20 gallon SS tank is replaced by a 10 gallon polypropylene unpressurized tank for better rear packaging, lighter weight, and translucent level visibility.
    A 24V diaphragm pump replaces the 12V pump for system voltage consistency. Dual stage inline filtration (50 micron + 5 micron) is added before the EWI to protect the atomizing nozzle and boiler surface.
    The EWI is upgraded to a high-pressure system with accumulator and solenoid injector rather than a simple drip module.
    Condenser loop unchanged: exhaust steam → condenser → liquid → tank return. Near-zero net water consumption at operating conditions.
    Preferred fill: distilled or deionized water. Emergency fill: clean tap water acceptable — note in service log for earlier filter and boiler inspection.
  </p>

