<!-- EWI MIST SYSTEM -->
<div class="panel" id="panel-ewi">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--inject)">Diagram 4 · High Pressure EWI Mist System — Phase 22</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">High Pressure Atomizing Mist · 100–300 PSI · Accumulator · Solenoid Injector · PID Control</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    The Phase 22 EWI system is fundamentally different from Phase 21. Rather than a low-pressure drip or simple injection, the water arrives at the boiler surface as a high-velocity ultra-fine mist at 100–300 PSI.
    The velocity of the mist droplets physically breaks through the Leidenfrost vapor cushion that would otherwise insulate droplets from the hot surface.
    A 0.5 liter pressure accumulator dampens the micro pump pulse cycle giving smooth constant pressure to the solenoid injector.
    The solenoid injector valve operates on microsecond timing similar to an automotive fuel injector — PID control loop reads boiler pressure and adjusts injection rate to maintain 90 PSI operating pressure.
    The atomizing nozzle is positioned at the top center of the boiler, angled 30–45 degrees to spray directly onto the copper pyramid apex.
  </p>

