  <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--elec)">Electrical System — Phase 22</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">24V System · Dual 2,500W Alternators · LiFePO4 48V Cold Start · Temple Heater Coil · Self-Sustaining</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    Phase 22 electrical system carries forward the Phase 21 24V architecture with one significant addition: the Miasma Temple Boiler Mark 1 internal heater coil.
    The heater coil draws 2,000–3,000W during cold start from the 48V LiFePO4 battery via a DC-DC converter.
    Once the engine reaches operating RPM the dual alternators supply 5,000W total. Boiler maintenance heater draw at operating temperature drops to approximately 500–800W (maintaining pyramid temp, not full cold-start heating).
    Net electrical surplus remains positive. The high-pressure EWI micro pump adds approximately 50–80W to the accessories load — well within the existing surplus.
    All Phase 21 drivetrain electrical components (PCW valves, BMS, charge controller, instrument cluster, wiring) are unchanged.
  </p>

