  <div class="new-box">
    <h4>▶ PHASE 22 ELECTRICAL BUDGET ANALYSIS</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>5,000W gross from dual alternators at operating RPM — same as Phase 21</li>
      <li>Temple heater maintenance draw: ~600W once pyramid is hot — significant reduction from cold start 3,000W peak which only lasts 15–20 seconds</li>
      <li>EWI hi-press pump: ~60W — small addition to accessories budget — well within surplus</li>
      <li>Solenoid injector: ~15W duty cycle averaged — negligible draw</li>
      <li>Total operating loads: ~600W heater + ~500W accessories + ~75W EWI + ~15W injector = ~1,190W total draw at steady state</li>
      <li>Net surplus at steady state: 5,000W - 1,190W = ~3,810W → charging LiFePO4 continuously</li>
      <li>DC-DC converter upgraded to 150A to handle 3,000W heater cold start peak safely</li>
      <li>All Phase 21 drivetrain electrical: PCW valves, BMS, charge controller, instrument cluster — all unchanged</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
