  <h2 class="section-title">Speed · Range · Torque — Temple Boiler · CVT Hydrostatic · Rear 2WD</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    Drivetrain is unchanged from Phase 21 — speed, torque, and range estimates remain similar. The Temple Boiler Mark 1 produces steam at the same 90 PSI operating pressure feeding the same two 75mm bore 250mm stroke pistons.
    Key improvements in Phase 22 affect cold start time (74 sec → 15–20 sec) and steam system reliability and maintenance intervals.
    Vehicle weight is slightly reduced: 10 gal poly tank is lighter than 20 gal SS tank saving approximately 40–45 kg. This marginally improves acceleration and traction. Estimated Phase 22 vehicle weight approximately 1,935–1,950 kg.
    The high-pressure EWI mist injection gives faster and more precise throttle response — the boiler pressure responds more immediately to injection rate changes versus the drip system in Phase 21.
  </p>

