  <div class="new-box">
    <h4>▶ PHASE 22 PERFORMANCE IMPROVEMENTS OVER PHASE 21</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Cold start 74 sec → 15–20 sec estimated: internal copper pyramid heater coil heats all levels simultaneously from inside out — copper thermal conductivity 25× faster than stainless</li>
      <li>Throttle response improvement: high-pressure mist EWI responds faster to pressure changes than low-pressure drip — boiler pressure tracks injection rate changes more tightly</li>
      <li>Vehicle weight reduced ~40–45 kg: 10 gal poly tank (4.5 kg dry) vs 20 gal SS tank (8 kg dry + extra water capacity) — marginally improves acceleration</li>
      <li>Flash conversion efficiency increased: cone + dome rivets break Leidenfrost layer — more water converts to steam per injection cycle — less water waste</li>
      <li>Boiler maintenance intervals extended: dual stage 50µm + 5µm filtration keeps boiler surface cleaner — slower scale buildup — longer service life</li>
      <li>Steam quality improved: standpipes guarantee dry steam exits — eliminates any residual water hammer risk from Phase 21 mid-height outlet positions</li>
    </ul>
