  <div class="warn-box">
    <h4>⚠ Phase 22 Temple Boiler Thermal Notes</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Copper pyramid runs significantly hotter than the SS shell — this is by design and is not a problem. The temperature gradient from pyramid to shell drives the flash process.</li>
      <li>Heater coil inside hollow pyramid: coil surface temperature (400–600°C) is well below nichrome rated limit (1,200°C) — ceramic insulation on leads is mandatory and must be inspected at each service</li>
      <li>EWI hi-press pump and accumulator must be mounted with thermal separation from the boiler — use a heat shield or standoff bracket — bladder material degrades above 80°C</li>
      <li>Cone and dome rivets are the same copper as the pyramid — thermally matched — no differential expansion stress concerns</li>
      <li>Domed SS 304 shell faces: the dome geometry distributes thermal stress better than flat faces — less warping risk over thermal cycles vs Phase 21 flat-face conventional boiler</li>
      <li>All Phase 21 drivetrain thermal notes (locked diffs, CVT cooler, oil bath sensors) remain in effect unchanged</li>
    </ul>
