  <div class="warn-box">
    <h4>⚠ Phase 22 Stress Notes</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Domed faces on the boiler significantly reduce hoop stress vs flat faces — same wall thickness now handles substantially higher pressure. Safety factor on domed faces is nearly double that of flat faces at same operating pressure.</li>
      <li>Atomizing nozzle: confirm manufacturer rating for 300 PSI water service before ordering. The 1.67× factor is tight — prefer a nozzle rated 500 PSI or higher for better margin.</li>
      <li>EWI accumulator bladder: EPDM or Buna-N both compatible with water at operating temps. Replace proactively at 3 years regardless of appearance — bladder failure releases pressure suddenly.</li>
      <li>EWI hi-press micro pump: confirm rated pressure and water compatibility before installing. Vibration from the steam engine may fatigue pump fittings — use vibration-damping mounts.</li>
      <li>Cone and dome rivets: primarily subject to thermal cycling stress rather than mechanical load. Inspect for cracking or loosening at each major service. Brazed or machined-integral rivets are stronger than pressed-fit — specify machined-integral on fabrication.</li>
      <li>Heater coil ceramic feedthrough is a critical pressure boundary component — seal must be pressure tested to 200 PSI before first run. Two feedthroughs minimum (one per heater terminal).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
