    <ul>
      <li>Heater coil thermocouple inside hollow pyramid: prevents coil from overheating if EWI injection rate exceeds flash capacity — auto cuts heater power above 500°C pyramid interior</li>
      <li>Shell surface thermocouple: monitors external SS 304 shell temperature — early warning if internal steam pressure is backing up without venting</li>
      <li>EWI supply pressure sensor: if filter clogs or pump fails, supply pressure to accumulator drops — warning triggers before injector starves boiler completely</li>
      <li>Accumulator overpressure PRV: if EWI micro pump over-pressurizes accumulator (pump fault), a small PRV on the accumulator vents excess pressure and pump auto-cuts</li>
      <li>Heater feedthrough pressure test: the two ceramic feedthroughs through the boiler bottom wall are new pressure boundary penetrations — mandatory pressure test to 200 PSI minimum before first steam operation</li>
      <li>Filter ΔP gauge on instrument cluster: driver-visible indication when filter cartridges need service — prevents loss of boiler protection from clogged filters</li>
    </ul>
