  <div class="warn-box">
    <h4>⚠ Phase 22 Cost and Build Notes</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Temple Boiler Mark 1 is the most machining-intensive component in the entire build — the hollow copper pyramid with machined-integral cone and dome rivets requires a skilled machinist and CNC time. Budget accordingly and get a firm quote before committing.</li>
      <li>Domed cube SS 304 vessel: custom fabrication required — no off-shelf unit. A pressure vessel fabricator with ASME experience is recommended. Specify all penetration locations before fabrication begins.</li>
      <li>Heater feedthrough is a critical pressure boundary — do not improvise. Use a rated high-temperature ceramic pressure feedthrough designed for this service. Mandatory pressure test before first steam operation.</li>
      <li>Phase 22 total estimate ~$36–40.5K vs Phase 21 ~$35–39K — marginal cost increase for significantly better cold start performance and steam system reliability</li>
      <li>Water tank savings: 10 gal poly tank (~$170) vs 20 gal SS (~$550) saves ~$380 and ~35 kg — partially offsets the temple boiler fabrication premium</li>
      <li>Atomizing nozzle: specify 400 PSI rated minimum — cheap nozzles will fail under EWI system pressure. Source from industrial spray nozzle suppliers, not automotive.</li>
      <li>EWI hi-press micro pump: consider a fuel injection transfer pump (rated for high pressure liquid service) or a miniature hydraulic pump as alternatives to purpose-built water injection pumps</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
